f China (1949-present). It guides students through pivotal events in modern Chinese history, and uncovers the origins of China's painful transition from a powerful early modern empire to a country torn by civil unrest and imperialist invasion, and then from a vanguard of world revolution to a post-communist party-state whose global power is on the rise.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(HA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2741, "crseId": 366677, "crseOfferNbr": 4, "subject": "CAPS", "catalogNbr": "2262", "titleShort": "Medicine and Healing in China", "titleLong": "Medicine and Healing in China", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 16629, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:55PM", "timeEnd": "04:10PM", "startDt": "08/29/2019", "endDt": "12/10/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "th289", "firstName": "Tj", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Hinrichs"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Mcgraw Hall 165", "bldgDescr": "McGraw Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "MCG165", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/29/2019", "endDt": "12/10/2019", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "ASIAN", "catalogNbr": "2262", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "BSOC", "catalogNbr": "2561", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "HIST", "catalogNbr": "2562", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "STS", "catalogNbr": "2561", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/29/2019", "sessionEndDt": "12/10/2019", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "An exploration of processes of change in health\u00a0care practices in China. Focuses on key transitions, such as the\u00a0emergence of\u00a0canonical medicine, of Daoist approaches to healing and longevity, of \"scholar physicians,\"\u00a0and of\u00a0\"traditional Chinese medicine\" in modern China. \u00a0Inquires into the development\u00a0of healing practices in relation\u00a0to both popular and specialist views of the\u00a0body and disease; health care as organized by individuals, families,\u00a0communities,\u00a0and states; the transmission of medical knowledge; and healer-patient\u00a0relations. Course readings\u00a0include primary texts in translation as well as\u00a0secondary materials.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "(GHB)", "catalogDistr": "(HA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2741, "crseId": 366971, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "CAPS", "catalogNbr": "2267", "tit